      },
      "fixed": "2.1.314",
      "url": "https://cursor.com/blog/claude-code-extension-security-notice",
      "note": "Cursor's notice (read 2026-11-01) names 2.1.312 and 2.1.313 for macOS and Windows, served by its marketplace from about 09:27 to 20:35 UTC on 29 Oct 2026, and gives one SHA-256 for their tampered extension.js. Anthropic published 2.1.312 on 27 Oct and no 2.1.313 anywhere (npm @anthropic-ai/claude-code, the VS Code Marketplace and Open VSX went from 2.1.312 to 2.1.314, read 2026-11-01), so 2.1.313 is listed for every editor and 2.1.312 only by that digest. Persistence the notice names: an SSH key labelled svc-telemetry in ~/.ssh/authorized_keys (on Windows also C:\\ProgramData\\ssh\\administrators_authorized_keys), ~/.config/.smt and ~/.config/.smtk, the LaunchAgent ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.apple.sysmond.plist (macOS), a crontab @reboot line running ~/.config/.smt (Linux), and the scheduled task SysMon or a Startup sysmon.cmd (Windows)."
    }
